UI QUALITY GATE (from Tope, mandatory for EVERY card that adds or changes any screen, widget, animation or admin page). Applies to mobile and admin.
Method: reference-led. Find the best real app example for the screen, reproduce its layout, flow and hierarchy closely, recolour with LingAfriq brand, add small upgrades. Never copy logos, icons, exact copy or code. Follow design-pack-mandatory; Rive work follows rive-designer-elite.
Score each criterion 0-10, strictly. Default to the LOWER score when unsure; 9 means a stranger would think it shipped from a top-tier studio; 10 is rare. Criteria: 1 visual hierarchy and layout; 2 typography and spacing grid (consistent tokens, no magic numbers); 3 colour and contrast (WCAG AA, brand-faithful); 4 motion and feedback (purposeful, 60fps on low-end phones, reduced-motion respected); 5 every state designed (loading, empty, error, offline, success, locked, child mode); 6 copy (human, warm, no placeholder or AI-sounding text); 7 accessibility (screen reader labels, tap targets 48dp, text scaling, RTL for Arabic/Darija); 8 consistency with the design system and sibling screens; 9 originality (does not look generic or template-made); 10 polish (no overflow, clipping, jank, misaligned pixels, on small and large phones).
PASS only if EVERY criterion is >= 9 AND the average is >= 9.0. Any criterion below 9: critique it in one line, fix, rescore. Maximum 3 revise loops; after that log the card in HANDOFF.md as UI-BELOW-BAR with scores and continue to the next card, never mark it Done.
Evidence required in the card's commit message body and HANDOFF.md: the 10 scores (one line, e.g. UI 9/9/9/10/9/9/9/9/9/9 avg 9.1), the reference app used, and widget/golden tests for key states. Self-scoring is checked by the reviewer, who rescores independently and may fail the card.
